Cyclowareness Sandbox schema migrations (Alembic).

Operator commands and the reason this directory exists are documented in the
header of ../alembic.ini. The service applies migrations itself at boot
(app.db.init_db), so these commands are only needed to upgrade, roll back or
adopt a database out of band.

Adding a revision:

    alembic revision --autogenerate -m "what changed"

env.py points autogenerate at app.db.Base.metadata and turns on batch mode for
SQLite, so a generated revision is valid on both SQLite and PostgreSQL. Review
it: autogenerate does not detect a table or column rename, and it will not
backfill a new NOT NULL column for rows that already exist.
